You have four tools and you are finishing a rebuild you can look at.

  measure(js, width, query)   runs a JavaScript arrow function in a real browser
                              against your page and returns what it evaluates to
  parent(js, width, query)    the same, against the original you are matching, so
                              you can read its measures instead of guessing them
  deploy(css, js)             splices your block in, publishes it, returns any
                              error the page throws
  done(summary)               when the checks pass, or when you are certain one
                              cannot pass and can say why

You have thirty steps and each one costs about fifteen seconds of browser time.
Spend them deploying and measuring. Do not read function sources looking for who
writes what: measure the effect, change it, measure again. The previous run spent
its last eight steps reading source and shipped nothing.

Your current block is on the page and is at the end of this brief. It replaces
itself on every deploy, so send it whole each time.

# Where it stands, measured

At 1440px, all passing:

    tab strip     79px      16 .vtab, 3 .vglab, 16 [role=tab]
    open rail    485px      children .gut, .track.two, one p.reading
    #count       inside .ipad, one element, no page error
    .card.land   none visible
    #noRows      renders

# The two faults, both at width 390

## 1. The page throws insertBefore, about a hundred and sixty times

    Failed to execute 'insertBefore' on 'Node': The node before which the new
    node is to be inserted is not a child of this node.

That is your move of #count into .ipad. Below 760px the page draws a different
instrument: `drawPhone` replaces the contents of #hero, so the .rails node you
are inserting before is no longer a child of the parent you are inserting into
by the time your observer fires. The observer then fires again on your own
mutation, and it repeats.

Two things to get right, not one. The insert has to check that the anchor is
still a child of the node it is inserting into, at the moment it inserts. And it
must not run on every mutation: if #count is already in the right place, do
nothing at all, so your own writes do not wake your own observer.

Decide what "the right place" is on a phone. The original at 390px keeps the
sentence at the top of the instrument, above everything the phone draws. Measure
the original at 390 and match where it puts it.

## 2. The body is three times wider than the window

    body scrollWidth 1,183 at innerWidth 390

Something inside the page is holding a fixed width. The original at 390 does not
scroll sideways at all. Find which element is over 390 wide, measure its width
and its parent's, and fix that element rather than putting overflow:hidden on the
body, which hides the fault instead of removing it.

# The checks, all of them, before you call done

  1. At 390: no page error at all, and body scrollWidth equal to innerWidth.
  2. At 390: no .rail visible, the phone layout only.
  3. At 1440: #vstrip at or under 130px with 16 .vtab, 3 .vglab, 16 [role=tab].
  4. At 1440: the open rail at or under 560px.
  5. At 1440: #count inside .ipad, exactly one element with that id, no error.
  6. At 1440 and 390: no visible .card.land, and #noRows still renders.
  7. At 1440: body scrollHeight at or under 1,900. It is 2,270 now. The original
     is 1,687. Take it out of spacing, never by hiding content.
  8. Still there at both widths: 18 controls in #sdControls, 18 buttons in
     #starters, 4 .rail, 16 section.panel.

Measure every one before you call done, and put the numbers in the summary.

Names on your page: #count.sdcount is the standing sentence, #hero.instrument >
.ipad is the instrument's inside, .rails holds the four rails, #vstrip.vgroups >
.vg > .vglab + .vgbtns > button.vtab is the tab strip, section.panel are the
panels, table.reps is the record table.

Do not undo the phone layout, the case sheet overlay, the record stepper or the
aria-labels. Prefix every new name.

--- YOUR CURRENT BLOCK ---

